If AI is unavailable, provide editable sample text and built-in templates.

## Native Android image generation

Render the final poster as an actual image using Android-supported drawing and image APIs.

Do not merely display a preview that cannot be exported.

Generate a high-resolution PNG suitable for saving and sharing.

Use Android MediaStore or an appropriate Android file-saving method.

Handle storage permissions correctly for the target Android version.

Show a clear success message after saving.

Allow the user to share the saved image through Android's native share sheet.

The poster generator must work without requiring a paid external image-generation service.

If additional image-generation services are available, treat them as optional enhancements rather than requirements.

## Impact data accuracy

For daily, weekly, and monthly impact posters:
- Retrieve figures from actual recorded activity data.
- Clearly identify the selected date range.
- Distinguish self-reported activities from verified activities.
- Never invent statistics to make a poster look impressive.
- Never present sample data as the user's real impact.
- Provide a useful empty-state poster when the user has no recorded activities.

Allow users to preview and edit their posters before saving.

